  "preamble": "Retroflexion and devoicing of the voiced alveolo-palatal fricative [ʑ] to [ʂ]. The documented case is the Middle Chinese 船 initial, reconstructed as [ʑ] (Baxter zy-) by Baxter, Zhengzhang and Pulleyblank, whose values for 船 and 禪 reverse the traditional rime-table assignment. In Mandarin most 船 words are read with sh-; a few level-tone words instead have aspirated ch- (see zh_palatal_to_ch_retroflex_aspirated).",
